.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt CLAUDE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm claude
.Nd Anthropic's Claude Code, a coding agent for the terminal
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar prompt
.Nm
.Fl p
.Ar prompt
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads and edits the files of the directory it starts in, runs shell
commands and
.Xr git 1 ,
and asks Anthropic's models what to do next.
With no
.Ar command
it starts an interactive session on the terminal, with the
.Ar prompt
as its first message when one is given;
.Fl p
answers one prompt on standard output and exits.
.Ql claude --help
lists the options and commands, and
.Ql claude Ar command Fl -help
describes one.
.Pp
The x86-64 GNU root has
.Nm
when it is built with the agents layer:
.Ql make ARCH=x86_64 GNU_AGENTS=claude os-real-gnu-ext2 ,
or
.Ql GNU_AGENTS=all ,
which the release to the installed machine uses.
The program is Anthropic's linux-x64 build of version 2.1.296, one
executable linked against glibc, installed unmodified.
.Pa /opt/claude/bin/claude
is the program, and
.Pa /usr/bin/claude
and
.Pa /bin/claude
link to it.
Claude Code is proprietary; Anthropic's notice, from the npm package of the
same version, is
.Pa /opt/claude/LICENSE.md .
The build fetches the program for the person who builds the image, and each
person signs in with an account of their own.
.Pp
.Ql claude doctor
reports two warnings that do not apply here: that
.Pa ~/.local/bin
is not on the path and that
.Pa ~/.local/bin/claude
is missing.
Those are where Anthropic's installer puts the program; this system
installs it under
.Pa /opt .
.Ss Signing in over SSH
.Nm
asks for a sign-in when it starts without one, and
.Ql claude auth login ,
or
.Ql /login
in a session, signs in again.
It prints an address at
.Lk https://claude.com
to open in a web browser.
The machine has no browser, so open that address on any other computer and
sign in there.
The browser cannot reach the callback that
.Nm
listens on, so it shows a code instead; paste the code at the
.Dq Paste code here if prompted
prompt.
.Ql claude auth login --console
signs in to an Anthropic Console account instead of a Claude subscription.
.Ql claude auth status
prints the method in use, and exits with status 1 when there is none;
.Ql claude auth logout
signs out.
.Pp
Instead of signing in, a Console API key in the environment variable
.Ev ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
is used as it is and not stored.
An interactive session asks once whether to use it and remembers the
answer;
.Fl p
uses it without asking.
.Pp
.Ql claude setup-token
takes the same browser sign-in, prints an OAuth token that is valid for a
year, and stores nothing.
Set
.Ev CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
to that token where no sign-in can be made, such as a script or a loop on
the machine.
It needs a Claude subscription and serves model requests only.
When several credentials are present,
.Ev ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
comes before
.Ev CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN ,
and both come before a sign-in.
.Ss Where the credentials live
A sign-in is kept in
.Pa ~/.claude/.credentials.json ,
with mode 0600.
The settings and the state of the projects are in
.Pa ~/.claude.json ,
and the sessions, their transcripts, the plugins and caches under
.Pa ~/.claude .
.Ev CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
names another directory in place of
.Pa ~/.claude ,
which keeps a second account apart.
.Ss Updates, telemetry and the sandbox
The managed settings,
.Pa /etc/claude-code/managed-settings.json ,
which come before a user's or a project's settings, set
.Ev DISABLE_UPDATES
to 1.
That stops the update a session would start in the background, and
.Ql claude update
and
.Ql claude install
print
.Dq Updates are disabled by your administrator
and change nothing, so the program stays the version the image has.
A new version comes with a new build of the root.
.Pp
.Nm
sends usage events to Anthropic and logs to Datadog, and fetches feature
flags from Anthropic, unless
.Ev DISABLE_TELEMETRY
is set to 1.
.Ev CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC
set to 1 stops those and the other requests that are not for the model or a
sign-in, such as the fetch of its change log, but for the download of
Anthropic's catalog of plugins, which
.Ev CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_OFFICIAL_MARKETPLACE_AUTOINSTALL
set to 1 stops.
.Pp
The sandbox that
.Nm
can run shell commands in needs bubblewrap, which this release does not
provide.
The managed settings turn it off, so the commands it runs have the user's
own rights, within what the permission mode of the session allows.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
a Console API key to use in place of a sign-in
.It Ev CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
a token from
.Ql claude setup-token
.It Ev CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
the directory to use in place of
.Pa ~/.claude
.It Ev HTTPS_PROXY
a proxy for every request
.It Ev NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS
a file of certificate authorities to trust besides those of
.Pa /etc/ssl/certs
.It Ev TMPDIR
where
.Nm
makes
.Pa claude-UID ,
its scratch directory, and
.Pa cc-socks ;
.Pa /tmp
when unset
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /opt/claude/bin/claude
the program
.It Pa /opt/claude/LICENSE.md
Anthropic's notice
.It Pa /etc/claude-code/managed-settings.json
the settings that turn updates and the sandbox off
.It Pa ~/.claude/.credentials.json
the sign-in
.It Pa ~/.claude.json
the settings and the state of each project
.It Pa ~/.claude
sessions, transcripts, plugins and caches
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success and 1 on an error, which includes
.Ql claude auth status
with no sign-in.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Sign in, then work in a repository:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ claude auth login
$ cd project
$ claude
.Ed
.Pp
Answer one prompt with a token made elsewhere by
.Ql claude setup-token :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ export CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=token
$ claude -p "Summarize the changes since the last tag"
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gh 1 ,
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1
.Pp
.Lk https://code.claude.com/docs "The Claude Code documentation"
